# Frontend JS Conventions

- Keep scripts lightweight and page-focused (no framework assumptions).
- Guard selectors before use (`if (!el) return;`) to avoid runtime errors on other pages.
- Match existing style (plain JS, small utilities, minimal abstraction).
- Avoid adding global state unless absolutely necessary.
- Preserve accessibility behavior when toggling UI (aria attributes, hidden states, focus order).
